# Chatmaxxing — Results Log

## Run 1 — Kaggle Single-Turn Data (Baseline)

**Dataset:** `data/tickets_clean.csv` (Kaggle customer support tickets)
**Tickets:** 30 before (range 500–529), 30 after (range 530–559)
**Prompt rule added by fix proposer:** *"If a customer's problem description is vague or incomplete, you MUST ask for clarification."*

| Phase | Failures |
|-------|----------|
| Before | 21/30 (70%) |
| After | 22/30 (73%) |
| Improvement | -1 (no improvement) |

**Clusters identified:**
- Agent assumed unspecified customer issue (8 tickets)
- Context Drift & Ungrounded Generation (6 tickets)
- Goal misidentification (7 tickets)

**Key finding:** Agent picked `[NEED_MORE_INFO]` on essentially every ticket. Manual trace review revealed the data was single-turn — there was no conversation history for the agent to use. Asking for clarification on a first message is correct behavior, not failure. **The eval/data mismatch was the bottleneck, not the prompt or the agent.**

---

## Run 2 — Twitter Multi-Turn Data

**Dataset:** `data/twitter_clean.csv` (1000 multi-turn conversations grouped from the Kaggle Customer Support on Twitter dataset, 4+ turns each)
**Tickets:** 20 before (range 30–49), 20 after (range 50–69)
**Prompt rule added by fix proposer:** *"Verify all factual statements against the provided context and adhere to established resolution processes."*

| Phase | Failures |
|-------|----------|
| Before | 12/20 (60%) |
| After | 11/20 (55%) |
| Improvement | +1 fewer failure |

**Clusters identified:**
- Factual inaccuracy and process error (6 tickets)
- Misunderstood primary customer intent (2 tickets)
- Agent generated unapproved tag (4 tickets)

**Key finding:** Multi-turn data gives the agent real context to work with. Clusters are noticeably more concrete (e.g. "agent generated unapproved tag" is a specific structural failure, not a vague intent issue). First positive improvement number observed in the project.

---

## Cross-Run Comparison

| Metric | Kaggle (single-turn) | Twitter (multi-turn) |
|--------|----------------------|----------------------|
| Failure rate | 70% | 60% |
| Disposition pattern | 100% `NEED_MORE_INFO` | Mixed dispositions |
| Cluster specificity | Vague | Concrete |
| Improvement signal | None / negative | Positive |

**Implication:** The eval framework correctly surfaced that single-turn data is a poor fit for this methodology. Same code, different data = different result. This validates the framework's diagnostic value beyond just measuring agent quality.

